		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Ride Stability:</strong> Open trailers ensure a smoother ride during braking or stopping, as the exposed nature of transport allows better distribution of vibrations.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Potential Damage:</strong> Open trailers expose your bikes to various external factors, including weather conditions and potential theft, which can lead to more risks and damages compared to enclosed carriers.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Visibility Challenges:</strong> The uncovered nature of open trailers may make it harder to monitor your bikes during transportation.</span></li>
